Switching to LocalExecutor doesn’t avoid this in Airflow 3.1.x — the supervisor still calls the Execution API (task-instances/{id}/run). Your stacktrace shows the same path (airflow.sdk.api.client → httpx), so it’s still Airflow process → API server URL resolving to IPv6 / unsupported AF.

Right now your scheduler (LocalExecutor worker process) is trying to reach the API on an address like localhost/::1 or some hostname that resolves to IPv6 first, and the container/network doesn’t support IPv6 → Errno 97.

Fix it permanently (Podman): force IPv4 + explicit API base + execution API URL
1) Put these into /apps/airflow/.env

Add (or ensure) exactly:

AIRFLOW__API__BASE_URL=http://airflow-api-server:8080
AIRFLOW__CORE__EXECUTION_API_SERVER_URL=http://airflow-api-server:8080/execution/

2) Critical: remove per-service environment: overrides

In your compose, services like airflow-worker (and any others) that define environment: can override inherited env maps. Even if you use env_file, I want your runtime to be deterministic.

So:

Move DUMB_INIT_SETSID=0 into .env

Remove the environment: block from airflow-worker (and any others that override)

3) Restart the stack
podman-compose down
podman-compose up -d

Verify from inside the scheduler (since LocalExecutor runs there)
podman exec -it airflow-scheduler bash -lc '
echo "== BASE/EXEC ==";
env | egrep -i "AIRFLOW__API__BASE_URL|AIRFLOW__CORE__EXECUTION_API_SERVER_URL" || true;

echo "== DNS ==";
getent hosts airflow-api-server || true;

echo "== Health ==";
curl -sS -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}\n" http://airflow-api-server:8080/health || true;

python - <<PY
import socket
print("localhost:", socket.getaddrinfo("localhost", 8080))
print("airflow-api-server:", socket.getaddrinfo("airflow-api-server", 8080))
PY
'


If /health returns 200, the ConnectError should disappear.

If /health still fails: your external network likely isn’t giving name resolution

Because you use external: true network (airflow-pasta-net), sometimes DNS/aliasing behaves differently.

Quick check:

podman exec -it airflow-scheduler bash -lc "ping -c1 airflow-api-server || true; getent hosts airflow-api-server || true"

If name doesn’t resolve

Hard-pin the API server to its static IPv4 (you’re already doing this for postgres/redis).
Give the API server a fixed IP too:

airflow-api-server:
  networks:
    airflow-pasta-net:
      ipv4_address: 10.89.0.20


Then set in .env:

AIRFLOW__API__BASE_URL=http://10.89.0.20:8080
AIRFLOW__CORE__EXECUTION_API_SERVER_URL=http://10.89.0.20:8080/execution/


Restart again.

Optional hardening: disable IPv6 inside Airflow containers

Add under x-airflow-common (if allowed in your environment):

sysctls:
  net.ipv6.conf.all.disable_ipv6: "1"
  net.ipv6.conf.default.disable_ipv6: "1"

About the “state mismatch / queued vs failed”

That’s a side-effect of the supervisor getting SIGKILL after failing to call the Execution API (it retries, then dies). Once connectivity is fixed, that mismatch should go away.

